    description: "PHASE 2 of coverage-directed selection: union the coverage-selected tests into\nAFFECTED_TESTS at the existing union site in scripts/smart-test.\n\nStrictly safer than today by construction -- it can only ADD tests. That is\nwhy it precedes any narrowing.\n\nThe justification is NOT speed. It is whether EXTRA_FROM_COVERAGE ever catches\na real dependency the static import-graph slice missed. Coverage sees dynamic\ndispatch that the slice over-approximates or misses entirely; the warm demo\nalready showed the shape, selecting test_cli_explain.py for a change to\nedge_types.find_edge_type because explain looks edge types up at runtime. If\nthat generalises, this is a CORRECTNESS improvement that happens to be fast,\nand it stands on its own even if Phase 3 never lands.\n\nRemains local-only. CI never invokes scripts/smart-test."  # 4559
    fields: {}  # 4559
- op: discuss  # 307c
  at: '2026-08-17T02:00:14Z'  # 307c
  by: agent  # 307c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 307c
  clock: 2  # 307c
  nonce: 307c  # 307c
  message: "OWNER DECISION 2026-08-16: THE 30-COMMIT GATE DOES NOT APPLY TO THIS ITEM.\nProceed with Phase 2 now; the counter stays as Phase 3's evidence, not Phase 2's.\n\nWHERE THE BLOCK CAME FROM. WI-nipur's closing note ends \"NEXT: WI-kuliv (Phase\n2) stays blocked until the counter reaches 30 admissible commits.\" That sentence\nattached Phase 3's gate to Phase 2. The exit criterion it gates on is: over >=30\ncommits, did any test appear in MISSED_BY_COVERAGE that both RAN and FAILED --\na safety claim about DROPPING a test. Phase 2 is additive only; it unions\ncoverage-selected tests INTO AFFECTED_TESTS and cannot drop anything. This\nitem's own description already says so (\"Strictly safer than today by\nconstruction -- it can only ADD tests. That is why it precedes any narrowing\").\nSo the counter measures a risk Phase 2 structurally cannot incur.\n\nTHIS ITEM'S ACTUAL JUSTIFICATION IS ALREADY EVIDENCED. The stated question is\nwhether EXTRA_FROM_COVERAGE ever catches a real dependency the static\nimport-graph slice missed. Read off the shadow log (10 observations, 2026-08-14\nto 08-16):\n\n    informative                        10 / 10  (100%)\n    dangerous misses                   0\n    runs where coverage ADDED a test   7 / 10   (309 extra files total)\n\nThe informative_rate worry recorded on WI-nipur -- that cold-index /\nall-new-code / collapsed-join observations would disqualify most rows and make\n\"30 commits\" a much longer wait than it sounds -- DID NOT MATERIALISE. Nothing\nhas been disqualified. 10 observations accrued over 25 dev commits in two days.\n\nOWNER'S RISK POSITION, recorded because it is what actually decides the gate\nrather than the statistics: a locally-missed test is a DELAYED catch, not an\nescape. Three independent backstops run the full set -- the per-PR Woodpecker\ngate, full-suite twice daily (01:00/13:00 UTC), and nightly (multi-Python\nmatrix + integration, which CD depends on) -- plus the stop-the-line protocol\nthat blocks PRs while full-suite is red. Against that, a 30-minute local cycle\ntime is the larger cost. \"We'd rather not miss tests locally, but we'd also\nrather not have 30-minute cycle times.\"\n\nCOST OF PHASE 2, STATED SO IT IS NOT A SURPRISE: it makes local runs SLOWER,\nnot faster -- roughly 44 extra test files per informative run against a 85-339\nbaseline. It is a correctness change that happens to cost time. The speed comes\nfrom Phase 3 (WI-bolot) and WI-hihuv; Phase 2 is the step that earns the right\nto narrow.\n\nONE FINDING FOR PHASE 3, recorded here because it changes WI-bolot's design and\nwas discovered while checking this. \"Remains local-only. CI never invokes\nscripts/smart-test\" is literally true and misleading in effect: CI does not\ninvoke the script, it CONSUMES ITS OUTPUT. .woodpecker/woodpecker.yml:380 says\n\"the committed .ci/affected-tests.txt manifest drives it\", and smart-test:1109\nwrites $AFFECTED_TESTS -- the same variable it runs. So narrowing that variable\nnarrows the MERGE-GATING CI as a side effect, not just the local run.\n\nDecoupling is one variable: keep $AFFECTED_TESTS (slice UNION coverage extras)\nfor the manifest, add a separate narrowed set for the local pytest invocation.\nLocal gets fast, the per-PR gate keeps today's recall, and a local miss costs\nminutes rather than a cron cycle. Cheap, and available whenever Phase 3 lands --\nnot a precondition, given the backstops above."  # 307c
