- op: discuss  # 393b
  at: '2026-08-17T03:13:52Z'  # 393b
  by: agent  # 393b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 393b
  clock: 5  # 393b
  nonce: 393b  # 393b
  message: "DECOUPLING LANDED, PR #387 (dev cd7534745e). Owner chose option A on 2026-08-16 and it is now structural rather than a note: smart-test captures MANIFEST_TESTS from AFFECTED_TESTS at a named seam, the manifest publishes MANIFEST_TESTS, and everything after the seam applies to the local run only. WHAT THIS MEANS FOR PHASE 2, concretely: union the coverage-selected tests into AFFECTED_TESTS BELOW the seam. Do NOT touch MANIFEST_TESTS. Above the seam is the static import-graph slice plus its declarative augmentations, and that is what the merge-gating CI runs. If Phase 2 had landed above the seam it would have added roughly 44 test files per informative run to what CI runs, making the per-PR gate slower while the local run was also slower -- the worst of both, and invisible in any test. Evidence: byte-identical manifests from HEAD's script and the new one over one tree (97 lines, only the timestamp differs); guard at packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_smart_test_manifest_split.py with positive controls including the exact 'simplify these two variables back into one' shape."  # 393b
