- op: discuss  # 2a7d
  at: '2026-08-17T06:22:50Z'  # 2a7d
  by: agent  # 2a7d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2a7d
  clock: 7  # 2a7d
  nonce: 2a7d  # 2a7d
  message: "PHASE 2 LANDED, PR #389 (dev 87fd5329a7). Wired exactly where the preceding note\nsaid: the union sits BELOW the seam, MANIFEST_TESTS is untouched.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED\n- coverage-select gains a `select` subcommand: same selection as `shadow`, but\n  BEFORE pytest instead of after, since a caller that intends to ACT needs the\n  answer when no junit exists yet.\n- smart-test unions its output into AFFECTED_TESTS below the seam, reporting\n  only the files the static selectors did not already have.\n- selectable_test_files() filters the selection against the filesystem. The\n  index is persistent, out-of-repo, and nothing prunes it on a rename; pytest\n  treats a missing path as a collection ERROR, not a skip. Unfiltered, a stale\n  entry would REDDEN a run this phase can only widen -- which would have broken\n  the additive-safety story outright.\n- SELECT_UNION is its own switch (--no-select-union), off in CI alongside the\n  shadow.\n\nNON-DESTRUCTION, MEASURED NOT ARGUED. The manifest this script writes is\nBYTE-IDENTICAL to the one the pre-Phase-2 script writes over the same tree,\ntimestamp excluded. Both scripts run against one tree, .ci/affected-tests.txt\nrestored between runs. The merge gate is untouched.\n\nTHE JUSTIFICATION REPRODUCES. On this tree a change to\nedge_types.find_edge_type selects test_cli_explain.py -- 4 files from 45 node\nids -- and test_cli_explain.py imports nothing the static slice could follow;\n`explain` looks edge types up at runtime. That is the item's stated question\nanswered on live data rather than from the shadow log.\n\nA DEFECT THIS PHASE INTRODUCED AND THIS PR FIXES, found by READING A LIVE RUN\nrather than by reasoning about the design. With the union wired, the shadow\nprinted \"actually selected: 90 / EXTRA_FROM_COVERAGE: 0\". That 0 is\nunfalsifiable: the union has already folded coverage's picks into\nAFFECTED_TESTS by the time the shadow compares against it. EXTRA_FROM_COVERAGE\nis the metric THIS ITEM IS JUSTIFIED BY (7 of the first 10 observations added a\ntest), so Phase 2 would have destroyed its own measurement, and the resulting\npermanent zero would have read as \"coverage stopped finding anything the slice\nmissed\". The shadow now compares against MANIFEST_TESTS -- the pre-union set,\nwhich is exactly what the first 10 observations were compared against, so the\nseries stays continuous across the phase boundary. Same shape as this project's\nother measurement tautologies (post-finalize is_resolved): the number is real,\nand it is measuring the instrument.\n\nGUARDS. test_smart_test_coverage_union.py EXECUTES the shipped shell block --\nlifted verbatim between its own if/fi -- against a stub selector, because a\nunion that quietly adds nothing satisfies every position check ever written. On\nthe day this landed a live run legitimately added ZERO (the slice already held\nall 3 picks), so a live run proves nothing either way; the off-switch case runs\nthe same stub and asserts the opposite outcome, which is what shows the ADD path\nfires. test_smart_test_manifest_split.py gains a position audit with its own\npositive controls, including the exact shape of a union placed one block early.\n\nONE INCIDENTAL FIX. The seam guard's block finder matched the nearest brace\ngroup ending in the manifest redirect, and `{` occurs all over ordinary shell\n(${BASELINE:-HEAD}, ${ARGS[@]}). The union block contains one, so the match\nstarted there and reported a violation in code unrelated to the manifest. It is\nnow anchored on the SELECTED_TESTS marker.\n\nCOST, as predicted: local runs get SLOWER. The time comes back at Phase 3\n(WI-bolot), which is next."  # 2a7d
